{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-75589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}11=3\\lambda  \\\\ 13=-2\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7ecfca31c0a02c61ffa14aeee33bc80637047bb29b2e10ed4ba4c0d4a20429c"} {"question" "q-75589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{13}{2}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{3}"] ["text" "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2=2\\lambda  \\\\ 3=-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7ecfca31c0a02c61ffa14aeee33bc80637047bb29b2e10ed4ba4c0d4a20429c"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-70917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=\\lambda  \\\\ -2=-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7ecfca31c0a02c61ffa14aeee33bc80637047bb29b2e10ed4ba4c0d4a20429c"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"] ["text" "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-106744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$  is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =5v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=5v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7ecfca31c0a02c61ffa14aeee33bc80637047bb29b2e10ed4ba4c0d4a20429c"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-36791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 10\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=4v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b7ecfca31c0a02c61ffa14aeee33bc80637047bb29b2e10ed4ba4c0d4a20429c"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["text" "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-107819" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/0269c9d60a97984f55cefccbd8cf1192dfdb4082935162206b1ce1a3cfb413f7.png)\n\nThe vector $u$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-1.$ Find the vector $Bu.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvector $u=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Bu & =-u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/afc3e8503656a84f23c7f58fd05e005ee07200b75ddec1aa5cf247b3484e81b4.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d1fa34c97a4729667f7b1d6e02285ec9d007bbdb486ea09c69045740fc58421"} {"question" "q-75734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/act